 "result_text": "`Chain.from_json(chain.to_json())` now works for chains that contain predicates. I checked a chain like the one in the issue, with `is_in` in `edge_match`. The round-trip gives back the same JSON. I didn't run the test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `graphistry/compute/ast.py`. When loading `filter_dict` and `edge_match` values, it called `ASTPredicate.from_json`. `ASTPredicate` is an abstract base class, so that call can't build a predicate. The repo already had a lookup that maps each predicate's `type` name to its class, in `graphistry/compute/predicates/from_json.py`, but `ast.py` wasn't using it.\n\nI imported that function into `ast.py` and used it in `maybe_filter_dict_from_json` (two lines changed). This applies to every place that function is used, including node filters and the source and destination node matches.\n\nI made no test changes and no commits.",
